        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "447acc07-858b-515b-87fd-756d2c463b29",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Bowdoin College, Brown University, WBOR, Colgate University, Hobart College\n- Places: Maine, Commonwealth of Massachusetts, Providence, Rhode Island, Brunswick, United States\n- People: Alva Kelley\n- Roles: head football coach\n- Topics: university founding, colonial colleges, college radio\n\nFacts:\n- Bowdoin College was chartered in 1794 when Maine was still part of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts.\n- Brown University was founded in 1764 as the College in the English Colony of Rhode Island and Providence Plantations.\n- Brown University is the seventh-oldest institution of higher education in the United States and one of the nine colonial colleges chartered before the American Revolution.\n- Brown University is a private Ivy League research university in Providence, Rhode Island, United States.\n- Alva Kelley served as head football coach at Brown University from 1951 to 1958.\n- Alva Kelley served as head football coach at Colgate University from 1959 to 1961.\n- Alva Kelley served as head football coach at Hobart College from 1963 to 1970.\n- Alva Kelley compiled a career college football record of 60–98–5.\n- WBOR (91.1 FM) is a radio station licensed to Bowdoin College in Brunswick, Maine, United States.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "b4627014-4ed3-5898-a4a6-12678338878a",
        "text": "Page: Bowdoin College. Sentence: At the time Bowdoin was chartered in 1794, Maine was still a part of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts.\nPage: Brown University. Sentence: Brown University is a private Ivy League research university in Providence, Rhode Island, United States.\nPage: Brown University. Sentence: Founded in 1764 as the College in the English Colony of Rhode Island and Providence Plantations, Brown is the seventh-oldest institution of higher education in the United States and one of the nine colonial colleges chartered before the American Revolution.\nPage: WBOR. Sentence: WBOR (91.1 FM) is a radio station licensed to Bowdoin College in Brunswick, Maine, United States.\nPage: Alva Kelley. Sentence: He served as the head football coach at Brown University (1951–1958), Colgate University (1959–1961), and Hobart College (1963–1970), compiling a career college football record of 60–98–5.",
